  "statement": "Two circles have centers that are \\(d\\) units apart, and each has diameter \\(\\sqrt{d}\\). For any \\(d\\), let \\(A(d)\\) be the area of the smallest circle that contains both of these circles. Find \\(\\lim _{d \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{A(d)}{d^{2}}\\).",
  "answerChoices": [],
